{"Using JavaScript-level addition (reminder.retryCount + 1) instead of Prisma's atomic increment operator creates race conditions when two scheduler instances run concurrently, causing one failure to be lost and weakening the delete after two failures logic": 0.810818612575531, "The second OR branch in the deleteMany query is missing a method guard, so it will delete any WorkflowReminder with retryCount > 1, not just SMS reminders - the cleanup should be scoped to SMS only": 0.9886078834533691, "The Twilio provider API call and database persistence are in a single try-catch, so if Twilio accepts the SMS but the database update fails, the error is treated as a send failure causing duplicate SMS on retry": 0.6471521258354187, "After multiple database failures, the reminder row may be deleted leaving orphaned jobs on Twilio with no database reference": 0.7239781618118286}